0.08 0.14 0.20 rg BT /F3 10 Tf 43 636 Td (and snapshots need separate qualification.) Tj ET
0.08 0.14 0.20 rg BT /F3 10 Tf 43 612 Td (McKusick's BSDCon 2003 UFS2 paper explains the motivation for a larger boot area,) Tj ET
0.08 0.14 0.20 rg BT /F3 10 Tf 43 598 Td (wider pointers, high-resolution timestamps and extended attributes. The design) Tj ET
0.08 0.14 0.20 rg BT /F3 10 Tf 43 584 Td (retains the cylinder-group FFS philosophy rather than adding a pooled CoW model.) Tj ET
